# The desktop is on by default, and `desktop off` / `desktop on` are
# remembered on the disk for the next boot.
@disk
$ desktop
desktop: on, the terminal window has 221x56 characters ('desktop off' ends it)
$ cat /system/desktop
/system/desktop: no such file or directory
$ desktop off
desktop off (saved)
$ cat /system/desktop
off
@reboot
$ desktop
desktop: off ('desktop on' starts it)
@screenshot 1920x1080 text
$ desktop on
desktop on (saved)
@reboot
$ desktop
desktop: on, the terminal window has 221x56 characters ('desktop off' ends it)
@screenshot 1920x1080 pixels 0,0=a8d0f0 1919,1079=a8d0f0 960,78=3a6ea5
